    "lineage": "TBD",
    "process_step": "#########\n# GDSC ETL is performed in two steps: shell script to ETL data into postgres\n# and then additional transformations with SQL in postGIS (if needed).\n####\n\n#########\n# Step 1 - bash script (pseudo code)\n####\n\n# create directory structure and move into it\nmkdir -p /data/mdc_sexual_predators/download -p /data/mdc_sexual_predators/etl\nchmod -R 777 /data/mdc_sexual_predators\ncd /data/mdc_sexual_predators\n\n# set update flag based on last update and update frequency\ndo_update=0 if date() < last_update + update_frequency else do_update = 1\n\n# download if update flag is set:\nif do_update == 1 then\nogr2ogr -nln mdc_sexual_predators download/mdc_sexual_predators.json 'https://services.arcgis.com/8Pc9XBTAsYuxx9Ny/arcgis/rest/services/SEXPRED_gdb/FeatureServer/0/query?outFields=*&where=1%3D1&outSR=4326&f=geojson 2>&1'\n\n# load into postGIS with:\nogr2ogr -lco GEOMETRY_NAME=geom -f PostgreSQL PG:\"<postgres connection>\" download/mdc_sexual_predators.json -nlt point -nln mdc_sexual_predators\necho success: mdc_sexual_predators.json loaded with ogr2ogr\n\n\n#########\n# Step 2 - SQL script (pseudo code):\n####\n\n# remove duplicate points and make geometries valid:\nUPDATE mdc_sexual_predators\n  SET geom=ST_MakeValid(ST_RemoveRepeatedPoints(geom));\n\n# add local geometry column and reproject existing geometries into local EPSG:\nALTER TABLE mdc_sexual_predators DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS geom_local CASCADE;\nSELECT AddGeometryColumn (\n  'mdc_sexual_predators',\n  'geom_local', 2236, 'point', 2\n);\nUPDATE mdc_sexual_predators\n  SET geom_local=ST_MakeValid(ST_RemoveRepeatedPoints(ST_Transform(geom,2236)));\nCREATE INDEX mdc_sexual_predators_geom_local_idx\n  ON mdc_sexual_predators\n  USING GIST (geom_local);\nNOTIFY pgrst, 'reload schema';\n# Move into corrrect directory and create derivative directory in data package on osgeo\ncd /data/mdc_sexual_predators/\nmkdir -p derived\n\n# Move into correct directory\ncd /data/mdc_sexual_predators/\n\n# Create pg_dump of table SQL in derivate directory on postgis.\npg_dump <postgres opts> -h gaia-db -t mdc_sexual_predators > derived/mdc_sexual_predators.sql\n\n# Create downloadable tarfile of SQL in derivative directory on postgis\nrm -f derived/mdc_sexual_predators.sql.tar.gz\ntar -czf derived/mdc_sexual_predators.sql.tar.gz meta_dcat_mdc_sexual_predators.json -C derived mdc_sexual_predators.sql\n\n",
    "processor": "GDSC automation (see Process Step)",
